Three blocks order three competing rules in a cycle: `a` puts hover before
focus, `b` focus before active, `c` active before hover. No two blocks
disagree on one pair, so there is no conflict, but no sheet order satisfies
all three. generate warns, names the blocks it overrides, and cuts the cycle
at one rule. A block bound to a name is named by its longident from
`[@@@css.bindings]` (found through the block's identity); an anonymous
block (here `c`, with no identity) by the `file:line` of its
`[@@@css.blocks]` entry. Each `[@@@css]` atom entry carries the key the ppx
computes: class, scope (specificity and subject), family, longhand mask and
descendant shape; a block lists its rules by index into the file's
`[@@@css]` entries.

  $ cat > m.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css ("._a_hov:hover{color:red;}", "_a_hov", "0,2,0 own", "color", 1, false)]
  > [@@@css ("._a_foc:focus{color:blue;}", "_a_foc", "0,2,0 own", "color", 1, false)]
  > [@@@css ("._a_act:active{color:green;}", "_a_act", "0,2,0 own", "color", 1, false)]
  > [@@@css.bindings [("M.a", "_id_a", "_a_hov _a_foc"); ("M.b", "_id_b", "_a_foc _a_act")]]
  > [@@@css.blocks [(5, "_id_a", [0; 1])]]
  > [@@@css.blocks [(6, "_id_b", [1; 2])]]
  > [@@@css.blocks [(7, "", [2; 0])]]
  > EOF

  $ styled-ppx.generate m.ml
  styled-ppx: the orders of block m.ml:7 form a cycle over competing rules; the sheet emits ._a_act:active{color:green;} after rules they put after it
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._a_hov:hover{color:red;}
  ._a_foc:focus{color:blue;}
  ._a_act:active{color:green;}

The cycle is cut at `:active`: of the rules that wait on one block edge, it
is the latest by definition order. The anonymous block `c` loses its order
(an element that is active and hovered gets `green`, not `red`).

Two named blocks that disagree on one pair are named by their longidents:

  $ cat > n.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css ("._a_hov:hover{color:red;}", "_a_hov", "0,2,0 own", "color", 1, false)]
  > [@@@css ("._a_foc:focus{color:blue;}", "_a_foc", "0,2,0 own", "color", 1, false)]
  > [@@@css.bindings [("N.first", "_id_f", "_a_hov _a_foc"); ("N.second", "_id_s", "_a_foc _a_hov")]]
  > [@@@css.blocks [(4, "_id_f", [0; 1])]]
  > [@@@css.blocks [(5, "_id_s", [1; 0])]]
  > EOF

  $ styled-ppx.generate n.ml
  styled-ppx: block N.first and block N.second put two competing rules in opposite orders (._a_hov:hover{color:red;} and ._a_foc:focus{color:blue;}); the sheet keeps their definition order
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._a_hov:hover{color:red;}
  ._a_foc:focus{color:blue;}

Only a rule on the cycle is cut. `x`, `y` and `z` order hover, focus and
active in a cycle; `w` puts `:disabled` before `:hover` and is not on the
cycle, so it keeps its order and the warning names only blocks on the
cycle:

  $ cat > p.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css ("._a_hov:hover{color:red;}", "_a_hov", "0,2,0 own", "color", 1, false)]
  > [@@@css ("._a_foc:focus{color:blue;}", "_a_foc", "0,2,0 own", "color", 1, false)]
  > [@@@css ("._a_act:active{color:green;}", "_a_act", "0,2,0 own", "color", 1, false)]
  > [@@@css ("._a_dis:disabled{color:gray;}", "_a_dis", "0,2,0 own", "color", 1, false)]
  > [@@@css.bindings [("P.x", "_id_x", "_a_hov _a_foc"); ("P.y", "_id_y", "_a_foc _a_act"); ("P.z", "_id_z", "_a_act _a_hov"); ("P.w", "_id_w", "_a_dis _a_hov")]]
  > [@@@css.blocks [(6, "_id_x", [0; 1])]]
  > [@@@css.blocks [(7, "_id_y", [1; 2])]]
  > [@@@css.blocks [(8, "_id_z", [2; 0])]]
  > [@@@css.blocks [(9, "_id_w", [3; 0])]]
  > EOF

  $ styled-ppx.generate p.ml
  styled-ppx: the orders of block P.z form a cycle over competing rules; the sheet emits ._a_act:active{color:green;} after rules they put after it
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._a_dis:disabled{color:gray;}
  ._a_hov:hover{color:red;}
  ._a_foc:focus{color:blue;}
  ._a_act:active{color:green;}

A disabled, hovered `w` element gets `red`, as `w` orders it.
